WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.077
This video reconstructs all twenty labs using narration, commands, and diagrams.

00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:08.676
It is not a live portal recording or a validation report.

00:00:08.676 --> 00:00:14.075
You will build a purchasing assistant using synthetic Contoso policies and inventory.

00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:20.759
The assistant retrieves evidence, checks stock, and prepares drafts, but never approves, orders, or pays.

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:26.479
The core path runs from module zero through twelve, followed by optional advanced modules.

00:00:26.479 --> 00:00:33.549
A successful command, a completed cloud execution, and a correct business answer are three different outcomes.

00:00:33.549 --> 00:00:38.742
Start by confirming the approved subscription, directory, region, and spending scope.

00:00:38.742 --> 00:00:45.171
Use separate folders for Korean and English, keeping the English language profile selected in its folder.

00:00:45.171 --> 00:00:48.880
Prepare Python, then run doctor and the synthetic data check.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.567
An administrator creates a uniquely named resource group and preserves its ownership receipt.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:01:01.552
Provision the project and models using the next module's requirements, then assign only the required scoped roles.

00:01:01.552 --> 00:01:06.312
Store endpoint and deployment names, not credentials, in the environment file.

00:01:06.312 --> 00:01:12.061
Portal sign-in and command-line authentication are separate, so verify the directory in both.

00:01:12.061 --> 00:01:16.313
Distinguish the product name, model version, and your deployment name.

00:01:16.313 --> 00:01:22.598
The target is GPT six Sol, with GPT four point one as judge and text embedding three small for vectors.

00:01:22.598 --> 00:01:28.082
Check regional catalog support, processing location, and available quota before deploying.

00:01:28.082 --> 00:01:36.586
For one learner, the starting recommendation is one hundred thousand tokens per minute for chat and judge, and ten thousand for embeddings.

00:01:36.586 --> 00:01:43.240
Convert these budgets using each model's actual capacity units, then read back both token and request limits.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.506
Run the bounded connectivity test only after approval.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:50.265
Throughput is neither a spending cap nor a quality guarantee.

00:01:50.265 --> 00:01:53.918
The first model call is the smallest connectivity exercise.

00:01:53.918 --> 00:01:58.641
Without the live flag, the command prints a plan and makes no cloud request.

00:01:58.641 --> 00:02:04.812
After checking configuration and authentication, send the default question once with the live flag.

00:02:04.812 --> 00:02:09.283
Inspect completion status, nonempty output, and the response identifier.

00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:14.762
You have not supplied company policy, so the model should not invent a purchasing limit.

00:02:14.762 --> 00:02:18.100
Do not keep resending until you get preferred wording.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:23.201
This step invokes a model; it does not yet create an agent or retrieve documents.

00:02:23.201 --> 00:02:27.988
Create a text agent with your model deployment and the supplied instructions.

00:02:27.988 --> 00:02:30.823
Do not attach knowledge or function tools yet.

00:02:30.823 --> 00:02:37.437
Ask about the laptop cap and real-time inventory; the agent should acknowledge that it cannot verify them.

00:02:37.437 --> 00:02:42.728
In one conversation, say you are considering a monitor, then ask which item you mean.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:46.003
Start a new conversation and ask the follow-up again.

00:02:46.003 --> 00:02:48.964
The earlier item should not silently carry over.

00:02:48.964 --> 00:02:54.381
Agent name, configuration version, conversation, and response identifiers are distinct.

00:02:54.381 --> 00:02:57.782
Reuse this agent in the next document-search exercise.

00:02:57.782 --> 00:03:01.336
Read the purchasing, expense, and security policies first.

00:03:01.336 --> 00:03:06.012
Attach file search to your existing agent and upload only those three files.

00:03:06.012 --> 00:03:11.499
Upload completion is not indexing completion, so wait until the documents are searchable.

00:03:11.499 --> 00:03:21.475
Ask about the laptop cap and replacement period, approvals and reimbursement for a two-point-nine-million-won purchase, and an undocumented German-branch policy.

00:03:21.475 --> 00:03:27.710
A filename in the answer is not enough: open the actual citation and compare its numbers and clauses.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.392
Undocumented rules should remain unverified.

00:03:30.392 --> 00:03:34.195
Retrieval augments the answer; it does not retrain the model.

00:03:34.195 --> 00:03:37.201
First run the stock and draft functions without AI.

00:03:37.201 --> 00:03:43.935
Two laptops total two million nine hundred thousand won, and the result remains a draft requiring human approval.

00:03:43.935 --> 00:03:49.587
Out-of-stock items, excessive quantities, and negative quantities must produce explicit errors.

00:03:49.587 --> 00:03:57.643
The integrated command then lets the model request a function name and arguments, while the program validates and executes the request.

00:03:57.643 --> 00:04:04.858
Compare the actual function output with the final answer: amount, required approvers, and the false order-submitted flag.

00:04:04.858 --> 00:04:07.864
A model's statement cannot grant business approval.

00:04:07.864 --> 00:04:11.532
Reuse the saved response for tracing and the capstone review.

00:04:11.532 --> 00:04:13.990
Use separate server and client terminals.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:18.599
Start the local inventory server and inspect its health and stock endpoints.

00:04:18.599 --> 00:04:22.163
Keep this unauthenticated practice server on loopback only.

00:04:22.163 --> 00:04:27.571
Next, discover the MCP tools and approve one call with the exact tool name and arguments.

00:04:27.571 --> 00:04:31.443
Omitting approval must block execution before the function runs.

00:04:31.443 --> 00:04:36.482
Cloud Toolbox and Skill registration are optional extensions after Search is ready.

00:04:36.482 --> 00:04:41.276
Distinguish discovering a tool, reading instructions, and actually invoking it.

00:04:41.276 --> 00:04:46.069
When finished, stop the local server rather than exposing it through a tunnel.

00:04:46.069 --> 00:04:50.056
Evaluation connects actual answers with criteria fixed beforehand.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:56.190
Compare instructions version one and version two using the same model, context, and twelve questions.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:00.791
Verify your ownership receipt and deployment, then collect each answer once.

00:05:00.791 --> 00:05:08.213
Only after collection completes should you submit the originals to native evaluation, without reinvoking the target model.

00:05:08.213 --> 00:05:12.997
Read completeness, relevance, groundedness, and the judge's reasons row by row.

00:05:12.997 --> 00:05:14.776
Preserve ties and regressions.

00:05:14.776 --> 00:05:24.836
Do not alter checklists or criteria after seeing the results to manufacture improvement, and do not treat this small exposed development sample as release approval.

00:05:24.836 --> 00:05:37.432
Keep the existing protection policy and test three harmless boundaries: inventing an undocumented branch limit, falsely claiming approval and ordering, and treating a document note as authority to bypass approval.

00:05:37.432 --> 00:05:40.640
Compare each response with the policy and tool records.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:45.869
A natural-language refusal and a function rejecting invalid input are different evidence.

00:05:45.869 --> 00:05:50.741
Model filtering does not replace business authorization or document access control.

00:05:50.741 --> 00:05:58.702
If you did not run a separate red-team assessment or document-level access test, do not claim those broader protections were verified.

00:05:58.702 --> 00:06:04.414
Evaluation asks whether the answer was good; tracing shows what happened during execution.

00:06:04.414 --> 00:06:11.409
Use the Application Insights connection established before the request to locate the same response identifier.

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:16.158
Compare agent version and time, then inspect search, model, and tool spans.

00:06:16.158 --> 00:06:22.575
Do not add child durations on top of their parent, or sum overlapping parallel spans as elapsed time.

00:06:22.575 --> 00:06:25.398
Missing logs mean unverified, not error-free.

00:06:25.398 --> 00:06:32.008
Instead of repeatedly invoking the model, first check the connection, query scope, and ingestion delay.

00:06:32.008 --> 00:06:37.324
For the capstone, open the response saved in module six with the local result reader.

00:06:37.324 --> 00:06:43.779
Review policy evidence, stock, amount, required approvers, and draft status without another cloud call.

00:06:43.779 --> 00:06:51.942
Compare the two-laptop calculation with the actual function output, and keep unverified conditions such as VAT inclusion explicit.

00:06:51.942 --> 00:06:54.726
Citations and tool results must be traceable.

00:06:54.726 --> 00:07:01.813
This review can complete the core purchasing task; Teams publication and Hosted deployment are not prerequisites.

00:07:01.813 --> 00:07:05.610
A completed draft is neither approval nor a completed order.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.245
Closing the browser does not stop billing.

00:07:08.245 --> 00:07:13.836
Stop only the sessions and routines you created, then read back those exact identifiers.

00:07:13.836 --> 00:07:20.776
Distinguish optional features that were never deployed, and do not overlook custom routine receipt filenames.

00:07:20.776 --> 00:07:25.532
Retaining resources can leave ongoing Search, logging, and storage charges.

00:07:25.532 --> 00:07:28.424
Empty billing rows do not establish zero cost.

00:07:28.424 --> 00:07:31.315
Record an owner and the next cost-review time.

00:07:31.315 --> 00:07:33.822
Delete only explicitly approved targets.

00:07:33.822 --> 00:07:38.577
After completing advanced modules, return to this same closeout procedure.

00:07:38.577 --> 00:07:44.323
Begin advanced retrieval by confirming that the three policies produce thirteen local sections.

00:07:44.323 --> 00:07:53.003
After an administrator prepares the approved Search service, generate embeddings, upload the sections, and create the index and knowledge base.

00:07:53.003 --> 00:07:57.404
Send the same question through keyword, hybrid, and Foundry IQ retrieval.

00:07:57.404 --> 00:08:03.212
Compare actual returned sections with their originals rather than ranking unlike numeric scores.

00:08:03.212 --> 00:08:07.491
This lab uses public synthetic policy and minimal extractive retrieval.

00:08:07.491 --> 00:08:12.564
It does not establish document-level user permissions or automatic answer synthesis.

00:08:12.564 --> 00:08:16.293
Search allocation can continue billing even without requests.

00:08:16.293 --> 00:08:19.751
A Hosted agent runs your own code in a managed runtime.

00:08:19.751 --> 00:08:28.779
Use the dedicated Python environment to package source, synthetic policies, and pinned dependencies, excluding secrets and evaluation answers.

00:08:28.779 --> 00:08:32.620
Even a local server can make billable model and Search calls.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:38.639
Deploy the code into the prepared project and grant only the runtime identity's required roles.

00:08:38.639 --> 00:08:45.042
Invoke the exact numeric remote version, then compare package contracts, tool outputs, and citations.

00:08:45.042 --> 00:08:52.405
Finally, stop the session compute while keeping the agent and resources according to the approved retention policy.

00:08:52.405 --> 00:08:59.425
In the separate Agent Framework environment, compare sequential, concurrent, group-chat, and handoff orchestration.

00:08:59.425 --> 00:09:07.861
Sequential connects author to reviewer; concurrent runs three independent roles; group chat returns the review to the author for revision.

00:09:07.861 --> 00:09:13.772
Handoff requires an actual delegation tool call, not merely a statement that delegation happened.

00:09:13.772 --> 00:09:18.883
Leave at least one minute between pattern starts and keep the call limits unchanged.

00:09:18.883 --> 00:09:23.932
Inspect transferred messages, role order, terminal state, tokens, and elapsed time.

00:09:23.932 --> 00:09:30.521
More agents do not automatically mean better quality, and these local roles are not remote routine targets.

00:09:30.521 --> 00:09:35.875
Store only one fictional preference: synthetic user A prefers table-formatted answers.

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:38.584
Do not use personal or employee information.

00:09:38.584 --> 00:09:45.009
Create the memory store, record the item identifier, and search separately in user A and user B scopes.

00:09:45.009 --> 00:09:47.591
A should retrieve that item; B should not.

00:09:47.591 --> 00:09:52.693
A table-formatted natural-language answer alone does not prove memory persistence.

00:09:52.693 --> 00:09:55.906
Item time-to-live differs from the store's lifetime.

00:09:55.906 --> 00:09:58.551
Delete an item only with separate approval.

00:09:58.551 --> 00:10:05.291
Under a no-deletion policy, report storage and isolation separately from the unperformed deletion exercise.

00:10:05.291 --> 00:10:07.791
A routine determines when an agent runs.

00:10:07.791 --> 00:10:15.482
Use the server-side file-search agent, distinguishing a disabled routine's manual dispatch from a genuine one-shot timer.

00:10:15.482 --> 00:10:23.942
Schedule one execution two minutes ahead, then verify the unique input marker, completed response, and trace within the bounded wait.

00:10:23.942 --> 00:10:28.877
Creation success or manual dispatch cannot substitute for scheduled execution.

00:10:28.877 --> 00:10:34.325
An empty CLI history page does not prove nothing ran; inspect the actual action trace.

00:10:34.325 --> 00:10:36.825
Finally, read back enabled equals false.

00:10:36.825 --> 00:10:42.593
Creating an Autopilot account or sending external messages is outside this timer exercise.

00:10:42.593 --> 00:10:46.851
Start enterprise governance with the synthetic local cache exercise.

00:10:46.851 --> 00:10:52.826
Observe the two expected failures: a denied user and a revoked user can still read cached data.

00:10:52.826 --> 00:10:57.656
Move authorization ahead of the cache return, then rerun the unchanged tests.

00:10:57.656 --> 00:11:01.152
Do not change the permitted-user list to make them pass.

00:11:01.152 --> 00:11:06.618
Next, distinguish developer, project identity, agent runtime, and end-user permissions.

00:11:06.618 --> 00:11:11.321
Document network, gateway, and document-access responsibilities separately.

00:11:11.321 --> 00:11:17.931
Passing the local exercise does not establish that real Azure roles or document permissions were tested.

00:11:17.931 --> 00:11:23.915
Finally, reproduce the local error that promotes a candidate solely because execution completed.

00:11:23.915 --> 00:11:31.033
Change only the function so promotion also requires a quality pass, zero critical failures, and zero missing rows.

00:11:31.033 --> 00:11:33.994
This exercise is not a real deployment approval.

00:11:33.994 --> 00:11:41.742
Build a release manifest connecting source and instruction hashes, model and agent versions, tools, responses, and evidence.

00:11:41.742 --> 00:11:45.774
Record when to retain or restore the previously approved version.

00:11:45.774 --> 00:11:51.506
Assign owners for model retirement and cost review, then return to module twelve's closeout.

00:11:51.506 --> 00:11:57.364
Keep source validation, deployment success, and release-quality approval separate throughout.
